Fig
===

This repository is a personal, offline-only fork of
aws/amazon-q-developer-cli-autocomplete, which is itself derived from the
autocomplete engine originally built by Fig (withfig). All of the AI, network,
telemetry and account features of the upstream project have been removed; what
remains is the terminal autocomplete dropdown and the shell integration that
feeds it. The upstream dual license is retained in full: this work is licensed
under either of LICENSE.APACHE (Apache License, Version 2.0) or LICENSE.MIT
(MIT license) at your option, and the upstream copyright notice in LICENSE.MIT
is kept as required by that license.

Vendored third-party code carries its own license alongside it:

  crates/macos-utils/accessibility-master/      MIT OR Apache-2.0, as declared
                                                in its own Cargo.toml
  packages/fuzzysort/                           MIT, Stephen Kamenar (LICENSE)
  packages/spec-types/                          MIT, Hercules Labs Inc. (Fig).
  packages/spec-generators/                     Vendored from the withfig/
  packages/spec-helpers/                        autocomplete-tools packages the
  packages/spec-compiler/                       specs used to depend on; each
                                                keeps its own LICENSE.
